# The app moved to app.podiumstack.com; this apex now serves the marketing
# site. Everything below keeps a link that was emailed, embedded or bookmarked
# when the app lived here working.
#
# Two things about this file's syntax that are easy to get wrong:
#
#   1. Exact paths are resolved by hash lookup and are free; every rule from
#      the first wildcard onward is a regex evaluated in file order. So static
#      rules go first.
#   2. `/portal/*` compiles to ^/portal/(?<splat>.*)$ and therefore does NOT
#      match a bare `/portal`. Every prefix needs a pair of rules.
#
# Query strings are carried across automatically, which is what makes the
# signed `/unsubscribe?t=…&sig=…` links and `/login?next=/portal/tasks` survive.
#
# Status codes are 302 for now, deliberately. A 301 is cached by browsers
# effectively forever, and moving the public event pages off the apex is a
# decision worth being able to walk back. Promote these to 301 once the move
# has soaked — it is a find-and-replace and a redeploy.

# --- exact paths ---
/login        https://app.podiumstack.com/login        302
/signup       https://app.podiumstack.com/signup       302
/logout       https://app.podiumstack.com/logout       302
/setup        https://app.podiumstack.com/setup        302
/unsubscribe  https://app.podiumstack.com/unsubscribe  302
/embed.js     https://app.podiumstack.com/embed.js     302
/portal       https://app.podiumstack.com/portal       302
/admin        https://app.podiumstack.com/admin        302
/review       https://app.podiumstack.com/review       302

# --- prefixes ---
/e/*          https://app.podiumstack.com/e/:splat          302
/portal/*     https://app.podiumstack.com/portal/:splat     302
/admin/*      https://app.podiumstack.com/admin/:splat      302
/review/*     https://app.podiumstack.com/review/:splat     302
/invite/*     https://app.podiumstack.com/invite/:splat     302
/embed/*      https://app.podiumstack.com/embed/:splat      302

# 308 rather than 302: these take POST/PUT/DELETE with bodies, and a 302 lets a
# client downgrade the method to GET. 308 preserves both method and body.
/files/*      https://app.podiumstack.com/files/:splat      308
/v1/*         https://app.podiumstack.com/v1/:splat         308
